== 7. Source ==
internal/wait/wait.go, woke: the wake's text is printed by Run itself, not through o.Fence,
and the result of the print is not checked. cmd/handoff/stuck.go, spareWake: MarkSent runs
before the text is returned. So reviewer-2's #853 point 1 follows from the code; I did not
run its paused case.
cmd/handoff/session.go, running(): a binding with no pid and a host is "not running" when
the host process has ended. stuckSeats takes !b.running() as the exact sign, so a host-only
binding (Codex) is covered by it (#853 point 3). Read, not run.
internal/status/status.go, Waiting: the same terms as the old WaitsFor, appended and sorted
where it took the maximum; WaitsFor is now the maximum of Waiting. No change in its result.
cmd/handoff/cmds.go, cmdAway: the cover question is asked whenever spareBinding() finds a
running spare; nothing reads that binding's block before asking (G2).
